# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Fiesta
# Ford Fiesta Mk2: a facelift of the Mk1 with a revised front end, on sale from
# late August 1983; production to February 1989. Britain's best-selling
# supermini of its era, with over 150,000 UK sales in its best year, 1987,
# beaten in the sales charts only by the Escort.
#
# Colours: Rosso Red, Ocean Blue, Diamond White, Black. The paint names are the
# actual Mk2 Ford offerings recorded from the Ford Cars brochures (Rosso Red
# 1984-89, Ocean Blue 1983-86, Diamond White 1983-89, Black 1983-89). The DVSA
# colour table starts at 1994 registrations, so its 1994-96 survivor shares
# (blue 23-25%, red 19-23%, white 7-10%, black 8-10%) are the measured base,
# adjusted for 1980s registrations, where red and white were stronger: red
# raised to 25%, white to 12%, blue to 24%, black 9%.
#
# Dates describe when that colour would be seen regularly on UK roads, not the
# production dates. Weights total 500, the 2026-11-15 anchor convention for the
# Fiesta (provisional; a central rebase follows), split 25:24:12:9.

